---js
{
  layout: "layouts/base.njk",
  ogType: "article",
  pagination: { data: "nhtsa.modelYears", size: 1, alias: "my", addAllPagesToCollections: true },
  permalink: (data) => data.my.url,
  eleventyComputed: {
    title: (data) => `${data.my.name} problems, complaints and recalls`,
    description: (data) => data.my.description,
    faqs: (data) => data.my.faqs,
    crumbs: (data) => [
      { name: "Home", url: "/" },
      { name: data.my.m.make, url: `/${data.my.m.makeSlug}/` },
      { name: data.my.m.model, url: data.my.m.url },
      { name: String(data.my.year) },
    ],
  },
}
---
{%- set s = my.s -%}
<p class="kicker"><a href="{{ my.m.url }}">{{ my.m.make }} {{ my.m.model }}</a> · model year {{ my.year }}</p>
<h1>{{ my.name }} problems, complaints and recalls</h1>
<p class="last-checked">NHTSA data checked {{ my.rec.checked | prettyDate }} · counts are computed from NHTSA's public APIs, not estimated</p>

<section class="quick" aria-labelledby="sum">
<h2 id="sum">Summary</h2>
{% for line in my.summary %}<p>{{ line }}</p>
{% endfor %}
{% if s.named.length and s.named[0].topicUrl %}
<p>Counts for {{ s.named[0].label | lower }} on other {{ my.m.model }} years, and the recalls whose component is {{ s.named[0].label | lower }}, are on the <a href="{{ s.named[0].topicUrl }}">{{ my.m.model }} {{ s.named[0].label | lower }} page</a>.</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

<div class="stats" role="list">
  <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b>{{ s.total | n }}</b><span>owner complaints</span></div>
  <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b>{{ s.recalls.length }}</b><span>recall campaigns</span></div>
  <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b>{{ s.crash | n }}</b><span>complaint{% if s.crash != 1 %}s{% endif %} reporting a crash</span></div>
  <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b>{{ s.fire | n }}</b><span>complaint{% if s.fire != 1 %}s{% endif %} reporting a fire</span></div>
  <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b>{{ s.injuries | n }}</b><span>{% if s.injuries == 1 %}injury{% else %}injuries{% endif %} reported</span></div>
  <div class="stat" role="listitem"><b>{{ s.deaths | n }}</b><span>{% if s.deaths == 1 %}death{% else %}deaths{% endif %} reported</span></div>
</div>

{% if s.parkIt.length %}
<div class="warn"><p><strong>Park-it warning.</strong> NHTSA marks {{ s.parkIt.length }} recall{% if s.parkIt.length > 1 %}s{% endif %} for this model year ({% for r in s.parkIt %}{{ r.campaign }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}) with "park it" or "park outside" advice until the repair is done. Check your VIN at <a href="https://www.nhtsa.gov/recalls" rel="nofollow noopener">nhtsa.gov/recalls</a>.</p></div>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="components">Complaints by component</h2>
<p class="muted">Owners pick one or more component groups when they file. Share is the percent of the {{ s.total | n }} complaints that name the group.</p>
{%- set maxc = s.components | maxOf("count") -%}
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Component group (NHTSA label)</th><th class="num">Complaints</th><th class="num">Share</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for c in s.components %}<tr><td><strong>{% if c.topicUrl %}<a href="{{ c.topicUrl }}">{{ c.label }}</a>{% else %}{{ c.label }}{% endif %}</strong>{% if c.note %}<span class="compnote">{{ c.note }}</span>{% endif %}{% if c.topicUrl %}<span class="compnote">Compared across {{ my.m.model }} years</span>{% endif %}<span class="bar" style="width:{{ c.count | barw(maxc) }}%"></span></td><td class="num">{{ c.count | n }}</td><td class="num">{{ c.share }}%</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>

<h2 id="recalls">Recalls ({{ s.recalls.length }})</h2>
{% if s.recalls.length %}
<p class="muted">Newest first. Summary, risk and remedy are NHTSA's own recall text (a U.S. government record), shown as published. A recall applies only to the vehicles its notice names. The complaint counts above are a separate record and are not the number of vehicles affected. Your VIN lookup is the final word.</p>
{% for r in s.recalls %}
<article class="recall" id="r-{{ r.campaign }}">
<h3>NHTSA campaign {{ r.campaign }}{% if r.park_it %}<span class="tag">Park it</span>{% endif %}{% if r.park_outside %}<span class="tag">Park outside</span>{% endif %}</h3>
<p class="muted">Received {{ r.received | prettyDate }} · {{ r.component | comp }}{% if r.component | subcomp %} ({{ r.component | subcomp }}){% endif %}{% if r.over_the_air %} · fix can be sent over the air{% endif %}</p>
<p><strong>What's wrong:</strong> {{ r.summary }}</p>
{% if r.consequence %}<p><strong>Risk:</strong> {{ r.consequence }}</p>{% endif %}
{% if r.remedy %}<p><strong>Remedy:</strong> {{ r.remedy }}</p>{% endif %}
{% if r.has_potential_units %}
<p class="muted">NHTSA's <a href="{{ r.potential_units_source_url }}" rel="nofollow noopener">campaignNumber record</a> lists {{ r.potential_units | n }} potential units affected for campaign {{ r.campaign }} as a whole{% if r.campaign_vehicle_count > 1 %}, across {{ r.campaign_vehicle_count }} model rows in that record{% endif %}. That figure is not a complaint count and is not a count of every {{ my.name }}.</p>
{% endif %}
{% if r.topicUrl %}<p class="muted">Compared with other years on the <a href="{{ r.topicUrl }}">{{ my.m.model }} {{ r.component | comp | lower }} page</a>.</p>{% endif %}
</article>
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
<p>NHTSA's recall database lists no recall campaigns for the {{ my.name }} as of {{ my.rec.checked | prettyDate }}.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2 id="timeline">When the complaints were filed</h2>
<p class="muted">By the year the complaint reached NHTSA. A late rise often means a part wearing out with age or a problem drawing attention after a recall.</p>
{%- set maxy = s.filedByYear | maxOf("count") -%}
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Year filed</th><th class="num">Complaints</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for y in s.filedByYear %}<tr><td>{{ y.year }}<span class="bar" style="width:{{ y.count | barw(maxy) }}%"></span></td><td class="num">{{ y.count | n }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>

<h2 id="other-years">Other {{ my.m.model }} years</h2>
<div class="tablewrap"><table>
<thead><tr><th>Model year</th><th class="num">Complaints</th><th class="num">Recalls</th><th>Most-named component</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for y in my.m.years %}{% if not y.noRecords %}<tr{% if y.suspectGap %} class="flag"{% endif %}><td>{% if y.year == my.year %}<strong>{{ y.year }} (this page)</strong>{% elif y.featured %}<a href="/{{ my.m.makeSlug }}/{{ my.m.modelSlug }}/{{ y.year }}/">{{ y.year }}</a>{% else %}{{ y.year }}{% endif %}{% if y.suspectGap %} — NHTSA's API count looks incomplete{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ y.s.total | n }}</td><td class="num">{{ y.s.recalls.length }}</td><td>{{ y.s.named[0].label if y.s.named.length else "—" }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href="{{ my.m.url }}">All {{ my.m.make }} {{ my.m.model }} years compared →</a></p>

{% include "partials/faq.njk" %}

<section class="how">
<h2 id="read">How to read these numbers</h2>
<ul>
<li>Complaints are reports owners file with NHTSA. NHTSA does not confirm each one, and one problem can be reported more than once.</li>
<li>Counts are not adjusted for sales: a model that sold twice as many cars can collect twice the complaints without being worse per car.</li>
<li>Older model years have had more time to collect complaints.</li>
<li>A recall listed here may not cover every car of this model year. The complaint count is not the number of vehicles affected. Check your VIN at <a href="https://www.nhtsa.gov/recalls" rel="nofollow noopener">nhtsa.gov/recalls</a>.</li>
<li>If a recall shows a potential unit count, that number is from NHTSA's campaignNumber API for the whole campaign. It can include other models and years.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section class="sources" aria-labelledby="src">
<h2 id="src">Sources</h2>
<ol>
<li><a href="{{ my.rec.complaints_source_url }}" rel="nofollow noopener">{{ my.rec.complaints_source_title }}: {{ my.rec.nhtsa_make }} {{ my.rec.nhtsa_model }} {{ my.year }}</a> <span class="checked">checked {{ my.rec.checked }}</span></li>
<li><a href="{{ my.rec.recalls_source_url }}" rel="nofollow noopener">{{ my.rec.recalls_source_title }}: {{ my.rec.nhtsa_make }} {{ my.rec.nhtsa_model }} {{ my.year }}</a> <span class="checked">checked {{ my.rec.checked }}</span></li>
{% set withUnits = s.recalls | selectattr("has_potential_units") %}
{% if withUnits | length %}<li>Potential units affected, where a recall shows one, come from NHTSA's Recalls API (<code>campaignNumber</code>), linked on that recall. The figure is for the whole campaign. Checked {{ my.rec.checked }}.</li>{% endif %}
<li><a href="https://www.nhtsa.gov/nhtsa-datasets-and-apis" rel="nofollow noopener">NHTSA: Datasets and APIs</a> (what the APIs contain)</li>
</ol>
</section>
